  "id": "Compound::DB00277 - Gene::5141",
  "verbalization": "Theophylline is implicated in the regulation of Pde4a through multiple mechanistic pathways. Pathway 1 directly links Theophylline to Pde4c, which is involved in 3',5'-cyclic-amp phosphodiesterase activity, and this activity is associated with Pde4a. Pathway 2 provides a causal link between Theophylline and Hypoxic-ischaemic Encephalopathy, which is further linked to Aminophylline, which binds to Pde4a. Pathway 3 highlights the broader classification of Theophylline as a xanthine, which includes Aminophylline, both of which bind to Pde4a. These findings suggest that Theophylline exerts its effects on Pde4a through binding and subsequent modulation of phosphodiesterase activity, potentially influencing cellular signaling pathways. The integrated evidence supports a direct interaction between Theophylline and Pde4a, mediated through the binding of Aminophylline, which is a metabolite of Theophylline. The observed relationships are consistent with a mechanistic link, though the exact role of Theophylline in Pde4a regulation remains to be fully elucidated.",
